[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   Step 107 -- named-direction audit of the recovered axes.
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   The recovered boundary axis is reported on the comet side as the
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   cap-declaration axis (34,-13), the detached-sample axis
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   (49.9,-17), and the third-cohort free-scan direction (50,-50)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   measured in step 106.  A natural referee question is whether the
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   axis is "just" a named direction of the sky -- the galactic
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   geometry that drives the tide, the solar-motion apex, the CMB
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   dipole, the ecliptic poles, or the perihelion direction
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   published for the Planet Nine hypothesis.
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   This step tabulates the angular separation between each
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   recovered axis (and its antipode, since the field is bipolar)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   and a list of named astrophysical directions, all converted to
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   ecliptic coordinates from their published source frames:
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   galactic centre / anticentre      (l = 0, 180 deg; b = 0)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   north / south galactic poles      (b = +/-90 deg)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   solar apex (Dehnen & Binney 1998) (l = 56.24, b = 22.78)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   solar antapex                     (antipode of the above)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   galactic rotation direction       (l = 90, b = 0)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   CMB dipole apex (Planck)          (l = 264.02, b = 48.25)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   north / south ecliptic poles      (beta = +/-90 deg)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   Planet Nine perihelion direction  (Brown & Batygin 2021:
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   Omega=94, omega=147, i=30)
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   A uniform-direction Monte Carlo then answers the coincidence
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   question: what fraction of random bipolar axes come as close as
[2026-09-20 12:20:36 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 107]   the measured axis to ANY member of the named set?
